{"id":"5e51c0ca1041168de7aa9e096982aebaeebabd38","axis":"silent","repo":"vllm-project/vllm","sha":"5e51c0ca1041168de7aa9e096982aebaeebabd38","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/design/dbo.md","lines":["@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@"," "," ## Motivation"," ","-The core motivation of the DBO system in vLLM is to overlap the sparse all-to-all communication in the MoE layer with the surrounding computation. This system currently only targets DP+EP deployments.","+The core motivation of the DBO system in vLLM is to overlap the sparse all-to-all communication in the MoE layer with the surrounding computation. This targets DP+EP deployments. For TP deployments without expert parallelism, the `all-reduce-overlap` [schedule](#schedules) overlaps the TP all-reduces instead."," "," ## Introduction"," ","@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ Below is the overlap schedule that is currently implemented in vLLM."," "," ## Running with DBO"," ","-To enable the DBO system pass in the `--enable-dbo` argument to your vllm serve command. This must be run in conjunction with `--data-parallel-size N` where N is greater than 1 and `--enable-expert-parallel`. Additionally, there are two configuration knobs.","+To enable the DBO system pass in the `--enable-dbo` argument to your vllm serve command. To overlap the all-to-all, this must be run in conjunction with `--data-parallel-size N` where N is greater than 1 and `--enable-expert-parallel`. With tensor parallelism on one DP rank and no expert parallelism, `--enable-dbo` runs the `all-reduce-overlap` [schedule](#schedules) instead. Additionally, there are two configuration knobs."," "," * `--dbo-decode-token-threshold` the minimum number of tokens in a decode-only batch required to enable DBO for that batch"," * `--dbo-prefill-token-threshold` the minimum number of tokens in a batch containing at least one prefill required to enable DBO for that batch","@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ Note that there must be at least two GPUs visible in `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES`"," "," ## Limitations"," ","-DBO cannot be combined with LoRA, pipeline parallelism, prefill context parallelism, multimodal, encoder-decoder or hybrid models, or encoder-only models. CUDA graphs must be Full or disabled: the runner rejects `PIECEWISE`.","+DBO cannot be combined with LoRA, pipeline parallelism, prefill context parallelism, multimodal, encoder-decoder or hybrid models, or encoder-only models. Multimodal models are supported under `all-reduce-overlap`. CUDA graphs must be Full or disabled: the runner rejects `PIECEWISE`."," "," ## DBO Components"," ","@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@ For a step with `num_ubatches > 1`, the runner calls `UBatchRunner.prepare` to s"," "," ### UBatchRunner"," ","-`UBatchRunner`, in `vllm/v1/worker/gpu/ubatch_utils.py`, is built by `maybe_build_ubatch_runner` when DBO is enabled and there is more than one DP rank.","+`UBatchRunner`, in `vllm/v1/worker/gpu/ubatch_utils.py`, is built by `maybe_build_ubatch_runner` when DBO is enabled and there is more than one DP rank, or the [schedule](#schedules) is `all-reduce-overlap`."," "," The batch is sliced before its attention metadata is built. `prepare` splits the batch at the midpoint of the DP-padded token count. A uniform batch of multi-token queries (speculative decoding verification) is split on a request boundary instead, so that each microbatch stays a uniform decode. `prepare` then builds the attention metadata for each microbatch and stores it in that microbatch's own `ForwardContext`. A microbatch that falls entirely inside the padding has no query tokens, and runs like a dummy batch."," ","@@ -84,3 +84,12 @@ The `dbo_register_recv_hook` method registers a callback that can be returned by"," The `dbo_maybe_run_recv_hook` method runs a callback that’s set by the `dbo_register_recv_hook` function if that callback exists."," "," The `dbo_yield` method puts the current thread to sleep and wakes up the other UBatch thread.","+","+## Schedules","+","+`--dbo-schedule` selects what the two microbatches overlap. Left unset, it is `all-reduce-overlap` with tensor parallelism on one DP rank and no expert parallelism, and `dispatch-combine-overlap` otherwise. Both run on the same runtime (`UBatchContext`, the token thresholds); they differ in where the microbatches hand off.","+","+* `dispatch-combine-overlap` is the schedule above: the hand-offs are the all-to-all yield points inside the `FusedMoEModularKernel`, and one microbatch's dispatch / combine overlaps the other's compute.","+* `all-reduce-overlap` makes each TP all-reduce a hand-off, in `GroupCoordinator._all_reduce_out_place`: the all-reduce runs on the comm stream while the other microbatch computes. It needs tensor parallelism on one DP rank without expert parallelism.","+","+Under `all-reduce-overlap` there is no DP handshake: the runner decides per step by the thresholds alone, and a split step runs eagerly. No all-to-all backend is needed, and multimodal models are supported, since the vision encoder runs outside the split."],"additions":13,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/distributed/test_pynccl.py","lines":["@@ -536,6 +536,7 @@ def test_pynccl_suspend_resume_idempotent():","     comm.disabled = False","     comm._suspended = False","     comm.comm = object()","+    comm._stream_comms = {}","     comm.nccl = Mock()"," ","     comm.suspend()"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/v1/worker/test_dbo_pure_tp.py","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,211 @@","+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0","+# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project","+\"\"\"DBO under pure tensor parallelism (one DP rank, no EP), without GPUs.\"\"\"","+","+import threading","+from types import SimpleNamespace","+","+import pytest","+import torch","+","+import vllm.distributed.parallel_state as parallel_state","+import vllm.v1.worker.ubatching as ubatching","+import vllm.v1.worker.workspace as workspace","+from vllm.config import CUDAGraphMode, ParallelConfig, VllmConfig","+from vllm.sequence import IntermediateTensors","+from vllm.v1.worker.gpu.dp_utils import dispatch_cg_and_sync_dp","+from vllm.v1.worker.gpu.ubatch_utils import merge_ubatch_outputs","+","+","+def test_merge_tensors_concatenates_along_tokens():","+    a, b = torch.arange(6.0).view(3, 2), torch.arange(6.0, 10.0).view(2, 2)","+    assert torch.equal(merge_ubatch_outputs([a, b]), torch.cat([a, b]))","+","+","+def test_merge_recurses_into_tuples_and_lists():","+    # EAGLE3 returns (hidden, aux); DSpark returns (hidden, [aux, ...]).","+    h = [torch.full((2, 4), float(i)) for i in range(2)]","+    aux = [","+        [torch.full((2, 3), 10.0 + i), torch.full((2, 5), 20.0 + i)] for i in range(2)","+    ]","+    merged = merge_ubatch_outputs([(h[0], aux[0]), (h[1], aux[1])])","+    assert isinstance(merged, tuple) and isinstance(merged[1], list)","+    assert torch.equal(merged[0], torch.cat(h))","+    assert torch.equal(merged[1][0], torch.cat([aux[0][0], aux[1][0]]))","+    assert torch.equal(merged[1][1], torch.cat([aux[0][1], aux[1][1]]))","+","+","+def test_merge_keeps_none_and_intermediate_tensors():","+    assert merge_ubatch_outputs([None, None]) is None","+    parts = [","+        IntermediateTensors({\"hidden_states\": torch.ones(2, 4) * i}) for i in range(2)","+    ]","+    merged = merge_ubatch_outputs(parts)","+    assert merged[\"hidden_states\"].shape == (4, 4)","+","+","+def _parallel_config(tp=4, dp=1, ep=False, dbo=True, schedule=None):","+    # An explicit backend skips the GPU count check: CI may run this on one GPU.","+    return ParallelConfig(","+        tensor_parallel_size=tp,","+        data_parallel_size=dp,","+        enable_expert_parallel=ep,","+        enable_dbo=dbo,","+        dbo_schedule=schedule,","+        distributed_executor_backend=\"mp\",","+    )","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    (\"tp\", \"dp\", \"ep\", \"schedule\"),","+    [","+        (4, 1, False, \"all-reduce-overlap\"),","+        (4, 2, False, \"dispatch-combine-overlap\"),","+        (4, 1, True, \"dispatch-combine-overlap\"),","+        (1, 1, False, \"dispatch-combine-overlap\"),","+    ],","+)","+def test_default_dbo_schedule(tp, dp, ep, schedule):","+    assert _parallel_config(tp, dp, ep).dbo_schedule == schedule","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"kwargs\", [dict(dp=2), dict(ep=True), dict(tp=1)])","+def test_all_reduce_overlap_rejected_outside_pure_tp(kwargs):","+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"all-reduce-overlap\"):","+        _parallel_config(schedule=\"all-reduce-overlap\", **kwargs)","+","+","+def test_explicit_dbo_schedule_is_kept():","+    config = _parallel_config(schedule=\"dispatch-combine-overlap\")","+    assert config.dbo_schedule == \"dispatch-combine-overlap\"","+","+","+def _config(tp=4, dp=1, ep=False, spec=False, mm=False, enc_dec=False):","+    return SimpleNamespace(","+        model_config=SimpleNamespace(","+            is_multimodal_model=mm, is_encoder_decoder=enc_dec, is_hybrid=False","+        ),","+        parallel_config=_parallel_config(tp, dp, ep),","+        lora_config=None,","+        speculative_config=object() if spec else None,","+        compilation_config=SimpleNamespace(cudagraph_mode=CUDAGraphMode.FULL),","+        is_mm_encoder_only=False,","+    )","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    (\"kwargs\", \"rejected\"),","+    [","+        # pure TP: the vision encoder runs outside the split","+        (dict(mm=True), None),","+        (dict(spec=True, mm=True), None),","+        # anything that is not pure TP keeps the old restrictions","+        (dict(mm=True, dp=2), \"multimodal\"),","+        (dict(mm=True, ep=True), \"multimodal\"),","+        (dict(mm=True, tp=1), \"multimodal\"),","+        # encoder-decoder models stay out under pure TP too","+        (dict(enc_dec=True), \"multimodal\"),","+    ],","+)","+def test_dbo_unsupported_features(kwargs, rejected):","+    unsupported = VllmConfig._get_dbo_unsupported_features(_config(**kwargs))","+    if rejected is None:","+        assert unsupported == []","+    else:","+        assert any(rejected in u for u in unsupported), unsupported","+","+","+def _parallel(threshold_prefill=8192, threshold_decode=32768):","+    return SimpleNamespace(","+        use_ubatching=True,","+        dbo_schedule=\"all-reduce-overlap\",","+        num_ubatches=2,","+        dbo_prefill_token_threshold=threshold_prefill,","+        dbo_decode_token_threshold=threshold_decode,","+    )","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    (\"num_tokens\", \"uniform_decode\", \"allow\", \"expected_ubatches\"),","+    [","+        (16384, False, True, 2),  # prefill above its threshold: split","+        (4096, False, True, 1),  # below: whole","+        (16384, True, True, 1),  # a decode step uses the decode threshold","+        (16384, False, False, 1),  # the caller did not allow a split","+    ],","+)","+def test_single_dp_rank_splits_on_its_own(","+    num_tokens, uniform_decode, allow, expected_ubatches","+):","+    desc, sync = dispatch_cg_and_sync_dp(","+        None,","+        num_reqs=2,","+        num_tokens=num_tokens,","+        uniform_token_count=None,","+        dp_size=1,","+        dp_rank=0,","+        need_eager=True,","+        parallel_config=_parallel(),","+        allow_ubatching=allow,","+        uniform_decode=uniform_decode,","+    )","+    assert sync is None","+    assert desc.num_ubatches == expected_ubatches","+    if expected_ubatches > 1:","+        # a split step runs eager","+        assert desc.cg_mode == CUDAGraphMode.NONE","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize((\"num_ubatches\", \"expected\"), [(1, 0), (2, 1)])","+def test_workspace_id_shared_across_microbatches(monkeypatch, num_ubatches, expected):","+    # TP-only DBO on the V2 runner keeps one workspace set.","+    monkeypatch.setattr(workspace, \"dbo_current_ubatch_id\", lambda: 1)","+    manager = workspace.WorkspaceManager(","+        torch.device(\"cpu\"), num_ubatches=num_ubatches, num_lanes=1","+    )","+    assert manager._get_workspace_id() == expected","+","+","+def _ubatch_contexts(schedule):","+    return ubatching.make_ubatch_contexts(","+        num_micro_batches=2,","+        compute_stream=object(),","+        comm_stream=object(),","+        forward_contexts=[object(), object()],  # type: ignore[list-item]  # stand-ins","+        ready_barrier=threading.Barrier(3),","+        schedule=schedule,","+    )","+","+","+def test_dbo_enabled_for_a_schedule(monkeypatch):","+    # Checks that belong to one schedule (the MoE all-to-all hand-off) must","+    # not fire under another.","+    monkeypatch.setattr(ubatching, \"_SCHEDULE\", None)","+    _ubatch_contexts(\"all-reduce-overlap\")","+    assert not ubatching.dbo_enabled(\"all-reduce-overlap\")","+    monkeypatch.setattr(ubatching, \"_THREAD_ID_TO_CONTEXT\", {0: 0})","+    assert ubatching.dbo_enabled()","+    assert ubatching.dbo_enabled(\"all-reduce-overlap\")","+    assert not ubatching.dbo_enabled(\"dispatch-combine-overlap\")","+","+","+def test_all_reduce_hand_off_is_a_no_op_under_another_schedule(monkeypatch):","+    monkeypatch.setattr(ubatching, \"_SCHEDULE\", None)","+    ctx = _ubatch_contexts(\"dispatch-combine-overlap\")[0]","+    # The streams are stand-ins: a hand-off that ran would raise.","+    ctx.switch_to_comm_sync(\"all-reduce-overlap\")","+    ctx.yield_and_switch_from_comm_to_compute(\"all-reduce-overlap\")","+    assert ctx.current_stream is ctx.compute_stream","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"is_tp_group\", [True, False])","+def test_all_reduce_uses_device_communicator_outside_a_microbatch(","+    monkeypatch, is_tp_group","+):","+    # A step that is not split takes the normal all-reduce.","+    monkeypatch.setattr(ubatching, \"_THREAD_ID_TO_CONTEXT\", {})","+    group = parallel_state.GroupCoordinator.__new__(parallel_state.GroupCoordinator)","+    group.device_communicator = SimpleNamespace(all_reduce=lambda x: x + 1)","+    monkeypatch.setattr(parallel_state, \"_TP\", group if is_tp_group else None)","+    x = torch.ones(2)","+    assert torch.equal(group._all_reduce_out_place(x), x + 1)"],"additions":211,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"vllm/config/parallel.py","lines":["@@ -45,6 +45,7 @@ def get_min_num_redundant_experts(num_logical_experts: int, ep_size: int) -> int"," DataParallelBackend = Literal[\"ray\", \"mp\"]"," EPLBPolicyOption = Literal[\"default\"]"," DCPCommBackend = Literal[\"ag_rs\", \"a2a\"]","+DBOSchedule = Literal[\"dispatch-combine-overlap\", \"all-reduce-overlap\"]"," EPLBCommunicatorBackend = Literal[","     \"torch_nccl\", \"torch_gloo\", \"torch_xccl\", \"nixl\", \"pynccl\", \"symm_mem\""," ]","@@ -308,6 +309,13 @@ class ParallelConfig:","     threshold, microbatching will be used. Otherwise, the request will be","     processed in a single batch.\"\"\""," ","+    dbo_schedule: DBOSchedule | None = None","+    \"\"\"What one microbatch overlaps with the other's compute:","+    `dispatch-combine-overlap` its expert all-to-all, `all-reduce-overlap` its","+    TP all-reduces. `all-reduce-overlap` needs tensor parallelism on one DP rank","+    without expert parallelism and is the default there; everywhere else the","+    default is `dispatch-combine-overlap`.\"\"\"","+","     disable_nccl_for_dp_synchronization: bool | None = None","     \"\"\"Forces the dp synchronization logic in vllm/v1/worker/dp_utils.py ","     to use Gloo instead of NCCL for its all reduce.","@@ -1300,6 +1308,21 @@ def _verify_args(self) -> Self:","                 f\"be at least the number of microbatches ({self.num_ubatches}).\"","             )"," ","+        pure_tp = (","+            self.tensor_parallel_size > 1","+            and self.data_parallel_size == 1","+            and not self.enable_expert_parallel","+        )","+        if self.dbo_schedule is None:","+            self.dbo_schedule = (","+                \"all-reduce-overlap\" if pure_tp else \"dispatch-combine-overlap\"","+            )","+        elif self.dbo_schedule == \"all-reduce-overlap\" and not pure_tp:","+            raise ValueError(","+                \"dbo_schedule=all-reduce-overlap needs tensor parallelism on one \"","+                \"DP rank without expert parallelism.\"","+            )","+","         return self"," ","     def reconfigure_for_independent_dp_rank(self) -> None:"],"additions":23,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"vllm/config/vllm.py","lines":["@@ -2106,7 +2106,10 @@ def has_blocked_weights():","                 f\"cudagraph_mode={self.compilation_config.cudagraph_mode}\"","             )"," ","-        if self.parallel_config.use_ubatching:","+        if (","+            self.parallel_config.use_ubatching","+            and self.parallel_config.dbo_schedule != \"all-reduce-overlap\"","+        ):","             a2a_backend = self.parallel_config.all2all_backend","             if current_platform.is_rocm():","                 supported_backends = [","@@ -3415,6 +3418,7 @@ def _get_dbo_unsupported_features(self) -> list[str]:","         model_config = self.model_config","         parallel_config = self.parallel_config"," ","+        schedule = parallel_config.dbo_schedule","         if self.lora_config is not None:","             unsupported.append(\"dual batch overlap with LoRA\")","         if parallel_config.pipeline_parallel_size > 1:","@@ -3422,7 +3426,8 @@ def _get_dbo_unsupported_features(self) -> list[str]:","         if parallel_config.prefill_context_parallel_size > 1:","             unsupported.append(\"dual batch overlap with prefill context parallelism\")","         if model_config is not None and (","-            model_config.is_multimodal_model or model_config.is_encoder_decoder","+            (model_config.is_multimodal_model and schedule != \"all-reduce-overlap\")","+            or model_config.is_encoder_decoder","         ):","             unsupported.append(\"dual batch overlap with multimodal models\")","         if model_config is not None and model_config.is_hybrid:"],"additions":7,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"vllm/distributed/device_communicators/pynccl.py","lines":["@@ -176,6 +176,8 @@ def _init_comm(self, device: int | str | torch.device) -> None:","         assert isinstance(device, torch.device)","         self.device = device","         # nccl communicator and stream will use this device","+        # Streams with their own communicator; the others use self.comm.","+        self._stream_comms: dict[int, PyNcclCommunicator] = {}","         with torch.accelerator.device_index(device.index):","             self.comm: ncclComm_t = self.nccl.ncclCommInitRank(","                 self.world_size, self.unique_id, self.rank","@@ -249,6 +251,8 @@ def from_unique_id_bytes("," ","     def destroy(self):","         if self.available and not self.disabled:","+            for stream_comm in self._stream_comms.values():","+                stream_comm.destroy()","             # ncclCommAbort can block until all CUDA graphs that","             # captured NCCL ops on this comm are destroyed — and","             # those graphs are released later in this same main-","@@ -270,6 +274,20 @@ def _abort():","             self.available = False","             self.disabled = True"," ","+    def bind_stream(self, stream: torch.cuda.Stream) -> None:","+        \"\"\"Give the collectives issued on `stream` their own communicator, so","+        they never share one with collectives on a concurrent stream. Collective.\"\"\"","+        if self.disabled or stream.cuda_stream in self._stream_comms:","+            return","+        assert self.group is not None","+        self._stream_comms[stream.cuda_stream] = PyNcclCommunicator(","+            self.group, self.device","+        )","+","+    def _comm_for(self, stream) -> ncclComm_t:","+        stream_comm = self._stream_comms.get(stream.cuda_stream)","+        return self.comm if stream_comm is None else stream_comm.comm","+","     def all_reduce(","         self,","         in_tensor: torch.Tensor,","@@ -298,7 +316,7 @@ def all_reduce(","             in_tensor.numel(),","             ncclDataTypeEnum.from_torch(in_tensor.dtype),","             ncclRedOpTypeEnum.from_torch(op),","-            self.comm,","+            self._comm_for(stream),","             cudaStream_t(stream.cuda_stream),","         )","         return out_tensor","@@ -322,7 +340,7 @@ def all_gather(","             buffer_type(output_tensor.data_ptr()),","             input_tensor.numel(),","             ncclDataTypeEnum.from_torch(input_tensor.dtype),","-            self.comm,","+            self._comm_for(stream),","             cudaStream_t(stream.cuda_stream),","         )"," ","@@ -355,7 +373,7 @@ def all_gatherv(","                 dst_slice.numel(),","                 ncclDataTypeEnum.from_torch(input_tensor.dtype),","                 root,","-                self.comm,","+                self._comm_for(stream),","                 cudaStream_t(stream.cuda_stream),","             )","             split_offset += split_size","@@ -385,7 +403,7 @@ def reduce_scatter(","             output_tensor.numel(),","             ncclDataTypeEnum.from_torch(input_tensor.dtype),","             ncclRedOpTypeEnum.from_torch(op),","-            self.comm,","+            self._comm_for(stream),","             cudaStream_t(stream.cuda_stream),","         )"," ","@@ -420,7 +438,7 @@ def reduce_scatterv(","                 ncclDataTypeEnum.from_torch(input_tensor.dtype),","                 ncclRedOpTypeEnum.from_torch(op),","                 root,","-                self.comm,","+                self._comm_for(stream),","                 cudaStream_t(stream.cuda_stream),","             )","             split_offset += split_size","@@ -449,7 +467,7 @@ def reduce(","             ncclDataTypeEnum.from_torch(input_tensor.dtype),","             ncclRedOpTypeEnum.from_torch(op),","             root,","-            self.comm,","+            self._comm_for(stream),","             cudaStream_t(stream.cuda_stream),","         )"," ","@@ -524,